{"success":true,"message":"Response generated successfully.","data":{"requestId":"977a29fd-2474-4021-8df3-2208dcbb77c9","response":"The `prompt` function in JavaScript is used to display a message in a dialog box, and wait for the user to enter some text before continuing execution of the program.

Here's an example:

```javascript
function checkPrompt() {
  var userInput = prompt("Enter your name:");

  if (userInput) {
    alert("Hello " + userInput);
  } else {
    alert("No input given");
  }
}

checkPrompt();
```

In this code, `prompt` will display a dialog box with the message "Enter your name:", and wait for the user to enter their name. The function then checks if any text was entered (i.e., not just pressed 'Cancel'). If something was entered, it displays an alert with a greeting; otherwise, it says "No input given"."},"timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:14:37.631451200Z"}

